###  http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/0f6af344-86b4-4a5c-ba8e-c41f3dba6b81
<http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/0f6af344-86b4-4a5c-ba8e-c41f3dba6b81> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                  :Evidence ;
                                                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/1a8f54a9-9c0b-43b6-8174-83bdaa5af4d0> ;
                                                                         rdfs:label """Gli scopi: […] 2. Ravvivare l’interesse e la comprensione del pubblico per l’arte e per i suoi problemi; 3. Promuovere lo studio dei problemi cittadini fondandone la determinazione sulla essenza della loro realtà ideale; 4. Studiare i problemi dell’insegnamento artistico che, per il ns. popolo, non devono essere secondi a quelli della tecnica; 5. Studiare i problemi dell’artigianato e delle scuole artigiane; 6. Difendere le opere d’arte, di storia e di cultura, patrimonio ideale del ns. popolo. […] L’azione:
[…] Interessare le istituzioni cittadine, gli enti locali, le industrie, i privati ad illustrare nobilitare ed arricchire le loro costruzioni in genere con opere d’arte."""@it ,
                                                                                    "The goals: […] 2. To revive public interest and understanding of art and its problems; 3. To promote the study of civic problems, basing their determination on the essence of their ideal reality; 4. To study the problems of artistic education, which, for our people, must not be secondary to those of technology; 5. To study the problems of craftsmanship and artisan schools; 6. To defend works of art, history, and culture, the ideal heritage of our people. […] The action: […] To involve civic institutions, local authorities, industries, and private individuals in illustrating, ennobling, and enriching their buildings in general with works of art."@en .


