###  http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/619b9f46-3471-43e1-a301-c1a950521dfa
<http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/619b9f46-3471-43e1-a301-c1a950521dfa> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                  :Evidence ;
                                                                         rdfs:label "[…] it is necessary, because it is our duty to let the Paduans know about their city, to let them know that Padua is one of the gems of Italy even if no one knows it, even if many pretend to ignore it and praise, for example, Siena and Perugia and Orvieto, etc., etc., which Padua has absolutely nothing to envy even if it has lost much of that marvelous moment of art that was constituted by the frescoes of the Ovetari Chapel by Mantegna. To the incredulous, I cite only these various and different testimonies: Scrovegni, Gattamelata, Basilica del Santo, Salone [...] And to return to the theme of Paduan modesty, you can get […] to see, for example, that the Salone, known for its unique size but located in the second tier compared to the Palladian Salone, is instead much more grandiose, more lively, more powerful"@en ,
                                                                                    "[…] è necessario, perché è doveroso far conoscere ai padovani la loro città far loro sapere che Padova è una delle gemme d’Italia anche se nessuno lo sa, anche se molti fingono di ignorarlo e vi esaltano p. es. Siena e Perugia ed Orvieto ecc. ecc. alle quali Padova non ha assolutamente nulla da invidiare anche se ha perso gran parte di quel meraviglioso momento d’arte che era costituito dagli affreschi della Cappella Ovetari del Mantegna. Agli increduli io cito solo queste diverse e differenti testimonianze: Scrovegni, Gattamelata, basilica del Santo, Salone [...] E per tornare al tema della modestia patavina voi potete arrivare […] a vedere p. es. che il Salone, noto sì per la unicità della mole ma collocato nei posti di secondo ordine rispetto al Salone palladiano è invece di tanto più grandioso, più vivo, più potente"@it .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/63aaf702-c16f-476f-9884-afa6a5c4d831
<http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/63aaf702-c16f-476f-9884-afa6a5c4d831> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                  :InterpretiveQuestion ;
                                                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/681d5e6a-bbcc-40fc-98ef-d18b4767ac76> ;
                                                                         rdfs:label "Esiste una relazione tra questo interesse dichiarato per il patrimonio artistico padovano e la presenza degli affreschi nei palazzi IRE?"@it ,
                                                                                    "Is there a relationship between this declared interest in Padua's artistic heritage and the presence of frescoes in the IRE buildings?"@en .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/6400d3ac-7c71-4c87-8e62-d871918c83d4
<http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/6400d3ac-7c71-4c87-8e62-d871918c83d4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                  :Evidence ;
                                                                         <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/3817f940-630f-4063-9c65-adb334a3115e> ;
                                                                         rdfs:comment "Example illustrating the distinction between an evidence and a textual passage. The evidence does not correspond to a specific text fragment, but to an interpretive construct intentionally identified by the interpreter through the close reading of one or more textual passages. In this example, the concept of \"Unification\" emerges from the interpretation of Carlo Rossi's book as a whole rather than from a single textual passage."@en ;
                                                                         rdfs:label "Carlo Rossi's concept of Unification"@en ,
                                                                                    "Il concetto di Unificazione di Carlo Rossi"@it .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/66310e30-0c27-4e6f-8af6-50259a651dcb
<http://www.semanticweb.org/int_r1/66310e30-0c27-4e6f-8af6-50259a651dcb> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                  :TemporaryInterpretiveConclusion ;
                                                                         rdfs:label "Il cantiere è concepito come progetto di ricostruzione industrialmente organizzato"@it ,
                                                                                    "The construction site is conceived as an industrially organised reconstruction project"@en .


